# Copy this file to .env and fill in a key. Only one is needed.
#
# Provider is auto-detected from the key's shape: a Groq key starts with
# "gsk_" and routes to the Groq-hosted models. Groq serves no embeddings
# endpoint, so retrieval is keyword-only on a Groq key alone -- point
# SQE_EMBEDDING_BASE_URL at a local embedder to get the vector path back.
# Any other key is treated as an OpenAI key and serves both from one endpoint.
#
# SQE_LLM_API_KEY is the preferred variable name going forward.
# OPENAI_API_KEY is still read as a fallback for compatibility with the
# original MVP's .env file.
SQE_LLM_API_KEY=

# Only the model-comparison matrix reads this one (`sqe matrix`). It is a
# separate slot rather than the key above because a matrix worth running spans
# providers, and the run must not silently measure one vendor four times.
# SQE_GROQ_API_KEY=

# --- Optional overrides (defaults are chosen per-provider automatically) ---
# SQE_GENERATOR_MODEL=
# SQE_SYNTHESIZER_MODEL=
# The model that grades narratives (`sqe judge`). Leave unset and the judge
# falls back to the synthesiser -- which means a model grading its own
# output, so set it to something else when the agreement number matters.
# SQE_JUDGE_MODEL=
# SQE_EMBEDDING_MODEL=
# Embeddings may come from a different endpoint than generation -- a hosted
# generator with no embeddings model plus a local embedder is a working pair.
# Both default to the generation endpoint, so leave them unset for one provider.
# SQE_EMBEDDING_BASE_URL=
# SQE_EMBEDDING_API_KEY=
# SQE_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# SQE_DUCKDB_PATH=
